   "html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Alpine Scenes</title>\n<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"sp-scheme\">\n{\n \"format\": \"sp-scheme-package\",\n \"spScheme\": \"2.0\",\n \"survey\": {\n  \"title\": \"Fractal Complexity in Alpine Scenes\",\n  \"description\": \"Faithful replication of the image-choice survey in Lavdas & Schirpke (2020), PLOS ONE 15(6):e0235257, with the authors' own Photoshop-manipulated Alpine scenes from Tyrol. For seven sets of two to four versions of the same view, participants pick the image they prefer and say why: most beautiful, most interesting, makes more sense or feels more familiar.\",\n  \"locale\": \"en\",\n  \"mediaFolders\": [\n   \"sets\"\n  ],\n  \"pages\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"sets\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"consent\",\n      \"name\": \"consent\",\n      \"title\": \"I have read the information above and agree to take part.\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"labelTrue\": \"Yes\",\n      \"labelFalse\": \"No\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"type\": \"custom\",\n      \"name\": \"choices\",\n      \"title\": \"Preferred image per set\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"description\": \"One row per image set (key = set1 … set7). Value { pick: letter of the chosen image as in the paper's figures (a, b, c, d), reasons: [subset of 'Most beautiful', 'Most interesting', 'Makes more sense', 'Feels more familiar'], positions: letters in the on-screen order }; shown = the image files in on-screen order. Sets: set1 (2 images): valley with an inserted fractal (a) or rectilinear (b) pattern; set2 (4 images): village with inserted graphics: Sierpinski carpet (a), rectilinear pattern (b), more advanced (c) and less advanced (d) fractal iteration of the letter E; set3 (2 images): village whose buildings are replaced by half Sierpinski carpets with Sierpinski-triangle roofs (a) or plain boxes with flat roofs (b); set4 (2 images): mountain stream unaltered (a) or with rocks replaced by copies of a few rocks and less varied vegetation (b); set5 (3 images): artificial stream with identical rocks (a), plus varied rocks and non-native plants (b), plus varied rocks (c); set6 (4 images): Alpine town view with an added building: two parts of the Golestan Palace, Tehran (a, b) or contemporary office buildings (c, d); set7 (4 images): Alpine river with an added building: ornate Eram Garden mansion, Shiraz (a), Bauhaus Dessau with windows filled dark (b), Bauhaus Dessau (c), simplified mansion (d); the paper's text and figure label these slightly differently, the figure labels are used. Analysis in the paper: share of respondents choosing each image per set, counts of each reason per image, paired t-tests between images.\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"about\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"gender\",\n      \"title\": \"What is your gender?\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": 1,\n        \"text\": \"Female\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 2,\n        \"text\": \"Male\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 3,\n        \"text\": \"Other\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 4,\n        \"text\": \"Prefer not to say\"\n       }\n      ]\n     },\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"age_group\",\n      \"title\": \"How old are you?\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": 1,\n        \"text\": \"Under 18\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 2,\n        \"text\": \"18–29\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 3,\n        \"text\": \"30–44\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 4,\n        \"text\": \"45–59\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 5,\n        \"text\": \"60 or older\"\n       }\n      ]\n     },\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"region\",\n      \"title\": \"Where do you live?\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": 1,\n        \"text\": \"Europe\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 2,\n        \"text\": \"Another part of the world\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 3,\n        \"text\": \"Prefer not to say\"\n       }\n      ]\n     },\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"place\",\n      \"title\": \"What kind of place do you live in?\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"description\": \"The paper asked for place of living and reports age groups, world region and settlement size in its S1 Table, without the exact categories; these categories are reconstructed.\",\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": 1,\n        \"text\": \"Large city\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 2,\n        \"text\": \"Small city or town\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 3,\n        \"text\": \"Village or countryside\"\n       }\n      ]\n     }\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n }\n}\n</script>\n<style>\n:root{--bg:#eef1f0;--card:#fff;--ink:#1b1f1e;--muted:#59625f;--accent:#2e5e4e;--accent-ink:#fff;--line:#d3dad7;--warn:#b3261e}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:16px/1.5 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif}\nmain{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:20px 16px 40px}\nh1{font-size:1.4rem;margin:0 0 10px}p{margin:0 0 12px;color:var(--muted)}\n.card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:16px;margin-top:14px}\n.btn{appearance:none;border:0;border-radius:10px;padding:12px 20px;font:inherit;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;background:var(--accent);color:var(--accent-ink)}\n.btn:disabled{opacity:.4;cursor:not-allowed}\n.q{margin-top:18px}.q>b{display:block;margin-bottom:4px}\nlabel.opt{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;padding:9px 12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;margin-top:6px;cursor:pointer;background:var(--card)}\n.top{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-bottom:8px}\n.t{color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.bar{height:5px;background:var(--line);border-radius:3px;overflow:hidden;flex:1;margin-left:12px;max-width:260px}.bar>i{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--accent)}\n.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px}\n.pick{appearance:none;border:3px solid transparent;border-radius:12px;padding:0;background:#ddd;cursor:pointer;overflow:hidden;position:relative;display:block;width:100%}\n.pick img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}\n.pick span{position:absolute;left:8px;top:8px;background:rgba(0,0,0,.6);color:#fff;border-radius:7px;padding:1px 9px;font-weight:700;font-size:.9rem}\n.pick.on{border-color:var(--accent);box-shadow:0 0 0 3px rgba(46,94,78,.25)}\n.qq{font-weight:600;margin:14px 0 6px}\n.err{color:var(--warn);margin-top:8px;min-height:1.2em}\n.credit{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 16px 24px;font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted)}\n@media (max-width:560px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main id=\"app\" aria-live=\"polite\"><p>Loading…</p></main>\n<footer class=\"credit\">Images: Lavdas &amp; Schirpke (2020), PLOS ONE 15(6):e0235257, doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0235257 (CC BY 4.0; base photos from Schirpke et al. 2013, CC BY 3.0). Used with credit for research; removed if the authors object.</footer>\n<script>\n(function(){\n  var KEY='lavdas2020:', SETS={\"1\": \"ab\", \"2\": \"abcd\", \"3\": \"ab\", \"4\": \"ab\", \"5\": \"abc\", \"6\": \"abcd\", \"7\": \"abcd\"}, REASONS=['Most beautiful','Most interesting','Makes more sense','Feels more familiar'];\n  var app=document.getElementById('app'), Q={}, byName={}, ans={}, done={}, pos={};\n  var NAMES=Object.keys(SETS);\n  function esc(s){return String(s==null?'':s).replace(/[&<>\"]/g,function(c){return {'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;'}[c];});}\n  function err(m){var e=app.querySelector('.err');if(e)e.textContent=m||'';}\n  function ok(r){return !(r&&r.ok===false);}\n  function load(k){try{return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY+k));}catch(e){return null;}}\n  function save(k,v){try{localStorage.setItem(KEY+k,JSON.stringify(v));}catch(e){}}\n  function saveAll(l,b,cb){Promise.all(l.map(function(a){return SPSite.answer(a[0],a[1]);})).then(function(rs){var bad=rs.filter(function(r){return !ok(r);})[0];if(bad){if(b)b.disabled=false;return err(bad.error);}cb();});}\n  function shuffle(a){a=a.slice();for(var i=a.length-1;i>0;i--){var j=Math.floor(Math.random()*(i+1)),t=a[i];a[i]=a[j];a[j]=t;}return a;}\n  function page(title,html,btn,cb){\n    app.innerHTML='<div class=\"card\">'+(title?'<h1>'+esc(title)+'</h1>':'')+html+'<div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">'+esc(btn||'Continue')+'</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=cb;\n  }\n  function radios(name){return (Q[name].choices||[]).map(function(c){return '<label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"'+name+'\" value=\"'+esc(c.value)+'\"> '+esc(c.text)+'</label>';}).join('');}\n  function val(n){var x=app.querySelector('input[name='+n+']:checked');return x?Number(x.value):null;}\n  function next(){\n    window.scrollTo(0,0);\n    if(!ans.intro)return intro();\n    for(var i=0;i<NAMES.length;i++){if(!done['set'+NAMES[i]])return trial(i);}\n    if(!ans.about)return about();\n    finish();\n  }\n  function intro(){\n    var miss=[];NAMES.forEach(function(k){SETS[k].split('').forEach(function(l){if(!byName['set'+k+'_'+l])miss.push('set'+k+'_'+l);});});\n    if(miss.length){app.innerHTML='<h1>Pictures missing</h1><p>Media folder sets must hold the 21 images; missing: '+esc(miss.join(', '))+'.</p>';return;}\n    page('Which view do you prefer?','<p>You will see '+NAMES.length+' sets of pictures of landscapes in the Alps. The pictures in a set show the same place with small differences. For each set, pick the picture you prefer and tell us why you chose it. It takes about 5 minutes.</p><p>Participation is voluntary and anonymous.</p><label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"ok\"> '+esc(Q.consent.title)+'</label>','Start',function(){\n      if(!document.getElementById('ok').checked)return err('Consent is needed to continue.');\n      var b=this;b.disabled=true;saveAll([['consent',true]],b,function(){ans.intro=true;next();});\n    });\n  }\n  function trial(i){\n    var k=NAMES[i], letters=pos[k], pick=null, n=0;NAMES.forEach(function(x){if(done['set'+x])n++;});\n    var g=letters.map(function(l,j){var f=byName['set'+k+'_'+l];return '<button type=\"button\" class=\"pick\" data-l=\"'+l+'\"><img alt=\"Picture '+(j+1)+' of this set\" src=\"'+esc(f.url)+'\"><span>'+(j+1)+'</span></button>';}).join('');\n    var r=REASONS.map(function(x,j){return '<label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"why\" value=\"'+j+'\"> '+esc(x)+'</label>';}).join('');\n    app.innerHTML='<div class=\"top\"><span class=\"t\">Set '+(n+1)+' of '+NAMES.length+'</span><div class=\"bar\"><i style=\"width:'+(100*n/NAMES.length)+'%\"></i></div></div>'+\n      '<div class=\"qq\">Which picture do you prefer? Tap it.</div><div class=\"grid\">'+g+'</div>'+\n      '<div class=\"qq\">Why did you choose this picture? You can tick more than one.</div>'+r+\n      '<div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Next</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div>';\n    app.querySelectorAll('.pick').forEach(function(x){x.onclick=function(){pick=x.dataset.l;app.querySelectorAll('.pick').forEach(function(y){y.classList.toggle('on',y===x);});err('');};});\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){\n      if(!pick)return err('Please tap the picture you prefer.');\n      var why=[].slice.call(app.querySelectorAll('input[name=why]:checked')).map(function(x){return REASONS[Number(x.value)];});\n      if(!why.length)return err('Please tick at least one reason.');\n      var b=this;b.disabled=true;\n      SPSite.answer('choices',{pick:pick,reasons:why,positions:letters.join('')},{key:'set'+k,shown:letters.map(function(l){return 'set'+k+'_'+l+'.jpg';})}).then(function(rr){\n        if(!ok(rr)){b.disabled=false;return err(rr.error);}done['set'+k]=true;next();});\n    };\n  }\n  var ABOUT=['gender','age_group','region','place'];\n  function about(){\n    page('About you',ABOUT.map(function(n){return '<div class=\"q\"><b>'+esc(Q[n].title)+'</b>'+radios(n)+'</div>';}).join(''),'Finish',function(){\n      var l=[];for(var i=0;i<ABOUT.length;i++){var v=val(ABOUT[i]);if(!v)return err('Please answer: '+Q[ABOUT[i]].title);l.push([ABOUT[i],v]);}\n      var b=this;b.disabled=true;saveAll(l,b,function(){ans.about=true;next();});\n    });\n  }\n  function finish(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h1>Thank you!</h1><div class=\"card\"><p>The pictures were edited to change one kind of visual complexity at a time: fractal versus simple graphics, the natural mix of large and small rocks and plants, and ornate older buildings versus plain modern ones. In the original survey of 144 people, the versions with fractal patterns, a natural scaling hierarchy or ornate pre-modern buildings were always preferred.</p><p style=\"font-size:.82rem\">Images and task: Lavdas, A. A., &amp; Schirpke, U. (2020). Aesthetic preference is related to organized complexity. PLOS ONE 15(6):e0235257, doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0235257. Used with credit and removed if the authors object.</p><p id=\"fin\">Submitting…</p><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    SPSite.complete().then(function(r){if(!ok(r)){err(r.error||'Some answers are missing.');var m=r.missing||[];setTimeout(function(){m.forEach(function(x){\n      if(x==='consent')ans.intro=false;else if(x==='choices')done={};else ans.about=false;});next();},1800);}\n      else{var s=document.getElementById('fin');if(s)s.textContent='Your answers have been saved. You can close this window now.';}});\n  }\n  SPSite.onReady(function(ctx){\n    ['consent'].concat(ABOUT).forEach(function(n){Q[n]=SPSite.getQuestion(n)||{};});\n    (SPSite.getMedia('sets')||[]).forEach(function(f){byName[f.name.replace(/\\.[^.]+$/,'')]=f;});\n    var p=load('pos')||{};NAMES.forEach(function(k){var L=SETS[k].split('');if(!p[k]||p[k].length!==L.length)p[k]=shuffle(L);});pos=p;save('pos',pos);\n    var a=(ctx&&ctx.answers)||{};\n    ((a.choices&&a.choices.trials)||[]).forEach(function(t){if(t.key)done[t.key]=true;});\n    if(a.consent===true)ans.intro=true;\n    if(a.place!=null)ans.about=true;\n    next();\n  });\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
